[[:db/retract 17592186246624 :answer-field/choices 17592186246520] {:db/id 17592186119822 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709" :question/id #uuid "973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709" :question/math-academy-id "q-34761" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 12{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=16 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second  equation yields\n\n$$\n12{x}_{2}+2(2)=16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(1)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+1+2=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3659e401-201b-5665-a817-8016820a5661"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3659e401-201b-5665-a817-8016820a5661" :answer-field/id #uuid "3659e401-201b-5665-a817-8016820a5661" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f2c222c-23e3-58cc-87ec-9f7920cb1f7d" "answer-b92f0488-96a7-580a-9581-5603eab3169c" "answer-0e83f3a8-e73e-5dcd-ac90-e7fbd7a63237" "answer-1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" "answer-ef9d08f1-fc9e-5876-bc5a-62f5443e92fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f2c222c-23e3-58cc-87ec-9f7920cb1f7d" :answer/id #uuid "6f2c222c-23e3-58cc-87ec-9f7920cb1f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b92f0488-96a7-580a-9581-5603eab3169c" :answer/id #uuid "b92f0488-96a7-580a-9581-5603eab3169c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e83f3a8-e73e-5dcd-ac90-e7fbd7a63237" :answer/id #uuid "0e83f3a8-e73e-5dcd-ac90-e7fbd7a63237" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" :answer/id #uuid "1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef9d08f1-fc9e-5876-bc5a-62f5443e92fe" :answer/id #uuid "ef9d08f1-fc9e-5876-bc5a-62f5443e92fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345147 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247248 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186246624 :answer-field/choices ["answer-b24cff0c-453c-54bf-b5a0-92ed0ff4ac54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b24cff0c-453c-54bf-b5a0-92ed0ff4ac54" :answer/id #uuid "b24cff0c-453c-54bf-b5a0-92ed0ff4ac54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" :question/id #uuid "ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" :question/math-academy-id "q-112247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(-3)=-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6dbd70cc-1860-587f-a06b-f6be24d7a7e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6dbd70cc-1860-587f-a06b-f6be24d7a7e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbd70cc-1860-587f-a06b-f6be24d7a7e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" "answer-de386f32-9648-5557-95da-e81b5a893cdb" "answer-5fac1657-f0bf-58cd-839a-2936f55e9617" "answer-922920ae-5499-5f5e-8c1f-2a7d78b98e5b" "answer-06febdbc-65f9-5901-99f7-6a7827495ba9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/id #uuid "a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de386f32-9648-5557-95da-e81b5a893cdb" :answer/id #uuid "de386f32-9648-5557-95da-e81b5a893cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fac1657-f0bf-58cd-839a-2936f55e9617" :answer/id #uuid "5fac1657-f0bf-58cd-839a-2936f55e9617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-922920ae-5499-5f5e-8c1f-2a7d78b98e5b" :answer/id #uuid "922920ae-5499-5f5e-8c1f-2a7d78b98e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06febdbc-65f9-5901-99f7-6a7827495ba9" :answer/id #uuid "06febdbc-65f9-5901-99f7-6a7827495ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247257 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -15 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -4 & -22\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 8{x}_{3}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-2$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-2)+1=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+5+(-2)=5.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7b9fccdb-a888-5b80-9f71-5e4ef95dcf8c" :activity/id #uuid "7b9fccdb-a888-5b80-9f71-5e4ef95dcf8c" :activity/title "Expressing the Coordinates of a Vector in a Given Basis" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050638 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-23a4ea36-89a6-56d3-bf56-d577c8099f1a" "step-620d8ecf-1f15-5e8d-9b5a-7ce1565395d4" "step-661bfcf4-d5c1-5b96-9534-b39e2fc11947" "step-f56d58dc-6376-5d83-8bb7-3af73050ef21" "step-500d3e2f-f405-56db-9c0b-61c6afc8b340"] :activity/first-step "step-23a4ea36-89a6-56d3-bf56-d577c8099f1a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-23a4ea36-89a6-56d3-bf56-d577c8099f1a" :step/id #uuid "23a4ea36-89a6-56d3-bf56-d577c8099f1a" :step/content "question-973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709" :step/next "step-620d8ecf-1f15-5e8d-9b5a-7ce1565395d4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-620d8ecf-1f15-5e8d-9b5a-7ce1565395d4" :step/id #uuid "620d8ecf-1f15-5e8d-9b5a-7ce1565395d4" :step/content 17592186345147 :step/next "step-661bfcf4-d5c1-5b96-9534-b39e2fc11947" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-661bfcf4-d5c1-5b96-9534-b39e2fc11947" :step/i